Changelog: 14-11-2026 23:58:33

Breaking. The BC250 Bazzite Suite is a repository of its own, github.com/RobertoTorino/bc250-bazzite (owner,
14-11-2026: one repository per suite, standalone with its own tooling, as the Bazzite Console Suite). Its files were
the folder bc250-bazzite/ of github.com/RobertoTorino/nexus and are now this repository's root: portal/, apps/,
docs/ with mkdocs.yml, icons/, install.sh and tools/. What it took from Nexus is its own now: core/ (bc250_core,
bundled in every app), the tools (the release and CI tools, the design panel and the disclaimer hook, the tours'
shared code and music, sync_icons.py, new_app.py), the development apps in dev/ (Nexus Dashboard, Nexus Release Tool,
Nexus Demo Recorder, Nexus Installer Tests, Nexus Sound Lab, Nexus Deps), test.sh and the root's files. The history
of these files stays in Nexus.

The releases are made here, with the same tags (<app>-v<x.y.z>, portal-v<x.y.z>), and the apps and the portal look
for them here; GitHub's Latest release is the newest portal. A portal or app installed from a release made in Nexus
keeps looking there and sees no newer release: installing the portal from this repository's latest release once
brings it here. The wiki is at robertotorino.github.io/bc250-bazzite/, built by this repository's docs.yml.

ci.yml runs every check on every push: the suite's and those that ran in Nexus's ci-nexus.yml (core, tools, dev/,
line endings, exec bits, the four files of every folder, workflows only at the root). release.yml is started by Nexus
Release Tool's Start new release on the release commit, or by hand (gh workflow run release.yml -f commit=...), and
waits for ci.yml alone. Gone with Nexus: the root's copy of portal/apps.toml (pin_app.py, suite_release.py,
check_manifest.py and new_app.py no longer write or compare it), the Nexus release and its version, the Nexus index,
the wait for ci-nexus.yml (tag-release.sh, release.yml, ci_local.py), make_icons.py and ICONS.md, and the tests of
Nexus's own rules for several suites. The tools find the suite at the root (tools/suites.py names it "."), and their
paths, the installer tests and the wiki's hooks are written for that layout.
